{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migrating-to-v8","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrating to V8"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table V8 was a major rewrite of React Table v7 from the ground up in TypeScript. The overall structure/organization of your markup and CSS will largely remain the same, but many of the APIs have been renamed or replaced."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"notable-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notable Changes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full rewrite to TypeScript with types included in the base package"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removal of plugin system to favor more inversion of control"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vastly larger and improved API (and new features like pinning)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better controlled state management"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better support for server-side operations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete (but optional) data pipeline control"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agnostic core with framework adapters for React, Solid, Svelte, Vue, and potentially more in the future"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New Dev Tools"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"install-the-new-version","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the new Version"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The new version of TanStack Table is published under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":" scope. Install the new package using your favorite package manager:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm uninstall react-table @types/react-table\nnpm install @tanstack/react-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"- import { useTable } from 'react-table' // [!code --]\n+ import { useReactTable } from '@tanstack/react-table' // [!code ++]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types are now included in the base package, so you can remove the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@types/react-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want, you can keep the old "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react-table"},{"type":"text","value":" packages installed so that you can gradually migrate your code. You should be able to use both packages side-by-side for separate tables without any issues."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"update-table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update Table Options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rename "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useReactTable"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The old hook and plugin systems have been removed, but they have replaced with tree-shakable row model imports for each feature."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"- import { useTable, usePagination, useSortBy } from 'react-table'; // [!code --]\n+ import { // [!code ++]\n+   useReactTable, // [!code ++]\n+   getCoreRowModel, // [!code ++]\n+   getPaginationRowModel, // [!code ++]\n+   getSortedRowModel // [!code ++]\n+ } from '@tanstack/react-table'; // [!code ++]\n\n// ...\n\n-   const tableInstance = useTable( // [!code --]\n-     { columns,  data }, // [!code --]\n-     useSortBy, // [!code --]\n-     usePagination, //order of hooks used to matter // [!code --]\n-     // etc. // [!code --]\n-   ); // [!code --]\n+   const tableInstance = useReactTable({ // [!code ++]\n+     columns, // [!code ++]\n+     data, // [!code ++]\n+     getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(), // [!code ++]\n+     getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(), // [!code ++]\n+     getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(), //order doesn't matter anymore! // [!code ++]\n+     // etc. // [!code ++]\n+   }); // [!code ++]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disable*"},{"type":"text","value":" table options were renamed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enable*"},{"type":"text","value":" table options. (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disableSortBy"},{"type":"text","value":" is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableSorting"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disableGroupBy"},{"type":"text","value":" is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableGrouping"},{"type":"text","value":", etc.)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"..."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"update-column-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update column definitions"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"accessor was renamed to either "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorKey"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorFn"},{"type":"text","value":" (depending on whether you are using a string or function)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"width, minWidth, maxWidth were renamed to size, minSize, maxSize"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optionally, you can use the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" function around each column definition for better TypeScript hints. (You can still just use an array of column definitions if you prefer.)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first parameter is the accessor function or accessor string."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The second parameter is an object of column options."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const columns = [\n-  { // [!code --]\n-    accessor: 'firstName', // [!code --]\n-    Header: 'First Name', // [!code --]\n-  }, // [!code --]\n-  { // [!code --]\n-    accessor: row => row.lastName, // [!code --]\n-    Header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code --]\n-  }, // [!code --]\n\n// Best TypeScript experience, especially when using `cell.getValue()` later on\n+  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', { //accessorKey // [!code ++]\n+    header: 'First Name', // [!code ++]\n+  }), // [!code ++]\n+  columnHelper.accessor(row => row.lastName, { //accessorFn // [!code ++]\n+    header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code ++]\n+  }), // [!code ++]\n\n// OR (if you prefer)\n+ { // [!code ++]\n+   accessorKey: 'firstName', // [!code ++]\n+   header: 'First Name', // [!code ++]\n+ }, // [!code ++]\n+ { // [!code ++]\n+   accessorFn: row => row.lastName, // [!code ++]\n+   header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code ++]\n+ }, // [!code ++]\n]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note: If defining columns inside a component, you should still try to give the column definitions a stable identity. This will help with performance and prevent unnecessary re-renders. Store the column definitions in either a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMemo"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useState"},{"type":"text","value":" hook."}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Option Name Changes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Header"},{"type":"text","value":" was renamed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Cell"},{"type":"text","value":" was renamed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":" (The cell render function has also changed. See below)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Footer"},{"type":"text","value":" was renamed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disable*"},{"type":"text","value":" column options were renamed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enable*"},{"type":"text","value":" column options. (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disableSortBy"},{"type":"text","value":" is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableSorting"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disableGroupBy"},{"type":"text","value":" is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableGrouping"},{"type":"text","value":", etc.)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortType"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"..."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changes to custom cell renderers"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" was renamed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getValue"},{"type":"text","value":" (Throughout the upgrade, instead of providing the value directly, a function "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getValue"},{"type":"text","value":" is exposed for evaluating the value. This change aims to improve performance by evaluating the value only when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getValue()"},{"type":"text","value":" is called and then caching it.)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell: { isGrouped, isPlaceholder, isAggregated }"},{"type":"text","value":" is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell: { getIsGrouped, getIsPlaceholder, getIsAggregated }"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column"},{"type":"text","value":": The base level props are now RT-specific. Values that you added to the object when defining it are now one level deeper in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDef"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table"},{"type":"text","value":": Props passed into the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":" hook now appear under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"migrate-table-markup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrate Table Markup"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender()"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.render('Cell')"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.render('Header')"},{"type":"text","value":", etc."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getHeaderProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFooterProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCellProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getRowProps"},{"type":"text","value":", etc. have all been "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deprecated"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table does not provide any default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"},{"type":"text","value":" or accessibility attributes like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role"},{"type":"text","value":" anymore. These are still important for you to get right, but it had to be removed in order to support being framework-agnostic."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You will need to define "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClick"},{"type":"text","value":" handlers manually, but there are new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get*Handler"},{"type":"text","value":" helpers to keep this simple."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You will need to define the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" props manually"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You will need to define the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"colSpan"},{"type":"text","value":" prop manually if using features that require it (grouped headers, aggregation, etc.)"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"- <th {...header.getHeaderProps()}>{cell.render('Header')}</th> // [!code --]\n+ <th colSpan={header.colSpan} key={column.id}> // [!code ++]\n+   {flexRender( // [!code ++]\n+     header.column.columnDef.header, // [!code ++]\n+     header.getContext() // [!code ++]\n+   )} // [!code ++]\n+ </th> // [!code ++]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"- <td {...cell.getCellProps()}>{cell.render('Cell')}</td> // [!code --]\n+ <td key={cell.id}> // [!code ++]\n+   {flexRender( // [!code ++]\n+     cell.column.columnDef.cell, // [!code ++]\n+     cell.getContext() // [!code ++]\n+   )} // [!code ++]\n+ </td> // [!code ++]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// in column definitions in this case\n- Header: ({ getToggleAllRowsSelectedProps }) => ( // [!code --]\n-   <input type=\"checkbox\" {...getToggleAllRowsSelectedProps()} /> // [!code --]\n- ), // [!code --]\n- Cell: ({ row }) => ( // [!code --]\n-   <input type=\"checkbox\" {...row.getToggleRowSelectedProps()} /> // [!code --]\n- ), // [!code --]\n+ header: ({ table }) => ( // [!code ++]\n+   <Checkbox // [!code ++]\n+     checked={table.getIsAllRowsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     indeterminate={table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     onChange={table.getToggleAllRowsSelectedHandler()} // [!code ++]\n+   /> // [!code ++]\n+ ), // [!code ++]\n+ cell: ({ row }) => ( // [!code ++]\n+   <Checkbox // [!code ++]\n+     checked={row.getIsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     disabled={!row.getCanSelect()} // [!code ++]\n+     indeterminate={row.getIsSomeSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     onChange={row.getToggleSelectedHandler()} // [!code ++]\n+   /> // [!code ++]\n+ ), // [!code ++]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"other-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other Changes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterTypes"},{"type":"text","value":" (now called "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":") have a new function signature as it only returns a boolean for whether the row should be included or not."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"- (rows: Row[], id: string, filterValue: any) => Row[] // [!code --]\n+ (row: Row, id: string, filterValue: any) => boolean // [!code ++]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"..."}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide is a work in progress. Please consider contributing to it if you have time!"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"migrating-to-v8","text":"Migrating to V8","level":2},{"id":"notable-changes","text":"Notable Changes","level":3},{"id":"install-the-new-version","text":"Install the new Version","level":3},{"id":"update-table-options","text":"Update Table Options","level":3},{"id":"update-column-definitions","text":"Update column definitions","level":3},{"id":"migrate-table-markup","text":"Migrate Table Markup","level":3},{"id":"other-changes","text":"Other Changes","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Migrating to V8\n\nTanStack Table V8 was a major rewrite of React Table v7 from the ground up in TypeScript. The overall structure/organization of your markup and CSS will largely remain the same, but many of the APIs have been renamed or replaced.\n\n### Notable Changes\n\n- Full rewrite to TypeScript with types included in the base package\n- Removal of plugin system to favor more inversion of control\n- Vastly larger and improved API (and new features like pinning)\n- Better controlled state management\n- Better support for server-side operations\n- Complete (but optional) data pipeline control\n- Agnostic core with framework adapters for React, Solid, Svelte, Vue, and potentially more in the future\n- New Dev Tools\n\n### Install the new Version\n\nThe new version of TanStack Table is published under the `@tanstack` scope. Install the new package using your favorite package manager:\n\n```bash\nnpm uninstall react-table @types/react-table\nnpm install @tanstack/react-table\n```\n\n```tsx\n- import { useTable } from 'react-table' // [!code --]\n+ import { useReactTable } from '@tanstack/react-table' // [!code ++]\n```\n\nTypes are now included in the base package, so you can remove the `@types/react-table` package.\n\n> If you want, you can keep the old `react-table` packages installed so that you can gradually migrate your code. You should be able to use both packages side-by-side for separate tables without any issues.\n\n### Update Table Options\n\n- Rename `useTable` to `useReactTable`\n- The old hook and plugin systems have been removed, but they have replaced with tree-shakable row model imports for each feature.\n\n```tsx\n- import { useTable, usePagination, useSortBy } from 'react-table'; // [!code --]\n+ import { // [!code ++]\n+   useReactTable, // [!code ++]\n+   getCoreRowModel, // [!code ++]\n+   getPaginationRowModel, // [!code ++]\n+   getSortedRowModel // [!code ++]\n+ } from '@tanstack/react-table'; // [!code ++]\n\n// ...\n\n-   const tableInstance = useTable( // [!code --]\n-     { columns,  data }, // [!code --]\n-     useSortBy, // [!code --]\n-     usePagination, //order of hooks used to matter // [!code --]\n-     // etc. // [!code --]\n-   ); // [!code --]\n+   const tableInstance = useReactTable({ // [!code ++]\n+     columns, // [!code ++]\n+     data, // [!code ++]\n+     getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(), // [!code ++]\n+     getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(), // [!code ++]\n+     getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(), //order doesn't matter anymore! // [!code ++]\n+     // etc. // [!code ++]\n+   }); // [!code ++]\n```\n\n- All `disable*` table options were renamed to `enable*` table options. (e.g. `disableSortBy` is now `enableSorting`, `disableGroupBy` is now `enableGrouping`, etc.)\n- ...\n\n### Update column definitions\n\n- accessor was renamed to either `accessorKey` or `accessorFn` (depending on whether you are using a string or function)\n- width, minWidth, maxWidth were renamed to size, minSize, maxSize\n- Optionally, you can use the new `createColumnHelper` function around each column definition for better TypeScript hints. (You can still just use an array of column definitions if you prefer.)\n  - The first parameter is the accessor function or accessor string.\n  - The second parameter is an object of column options.\n\n```tsx\nconst columns = [\n-  { // [!code --]\n-    accessor: 'firstName', // [!code --]\n-    Header: 'First Name', // [!code --]\n-  }, // [!code --]\n-  { // [!code --]\n-    accessor: row => row.lastName, // [!code --]\n-    Header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code --]\n-  }, // [!code --]\n\n// Best TypeScript experience, especially when using `cell.getValue()` later on\n+  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', { //accessorKey // [!code ++]\n+    header: 'First Name', // [!code ++]\n+  }), // [!code ++]\n+  columnHelper.accessor(row => row.lastName, { //accessorFn // [!code ++]\n+    header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code ++]\n+  }), // [!code ++]\n\n// OR (if you prefer)\n+ { // [!code ++]\n+   accessorKey: 'firstName', // [!code ++]\n+   header: 'First Name', // [!code ++]\n+ }, // [!code ++]\n+ { // [!code ++]\n+   accessorFn: row => row.lastName, // [!code ++]\n+   header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code ++]\n+ }, // [!code ++]\n]\n```\n\n> Note: If defining columns inside a component, you should still try to give the column definitions a stable identity. This will help with performance and prevent unnecessary re-renders. Store the column definitions in either a `useMemo` or `useState` hook.\n\n- Column Option Name Changes\n\n  - `Header` was renamed to `header`\n  - `Cell` was renamed to `cell` (The cell render function has also changed. See below)\n  - `Footer` was renamed to `footer`\n  - All `disable*` column options were renamed to `enable*` column options. (e.g. `disableSortBy` is now `enableSorting`, `disableGroupBy` is now `enableGrouping`, etc.)\n  - `sortType` `sortingFn`\n  - ...\n\n- Changes to custom cell renderers\n\n  - `value` was renamed `getValue` (Throughout the upgrade, instead of providing the value directly, a function `getValue` is exposed for evaluating the value. This change aims to improve performance by evaluating the value only when `getValue()` is called and then caching it.)\n  - `cell: { isGrouped, isPlaceholder, isAggregated }` is now `cell: { getIsGrouped, getIsPlaceholder, getIsAggregated }`\n  - `column`: The base level props are now RT-specific. Values that you added to the object when defining it are now one level deeper in `columnDef`.\n  - `table`: Props passed into the `useTable` hook now appear under `options`.\n\n### Migrate Table Markup\n\n- Use `flexRender()` instead of `cell.render('Cell')` or `column.render('Header')`, etc.\n- `getHeaderProps`, `getFooterProps`, `getCellProps`, `getRowProps`, etc. have all been _deprecated_.\n  - TanStack Table does not provide any default `style` or accessibility attributes like `role` anymore. These are still important for you to get right, but it had to be removed in order to support being framework-agnostic.\n  - You will need to define `onClick` handlers manually, but there are new `get*Handler` helpers to keep this simple.\n  - You will need to define the `key` props manually\n  - You will need to define the `colSpan` prop manually if using features that require it (grouped headers, aggregation, etc.)\n\n```tsx\n- <th {...header.getHeaderProps()}>{cell.render('Header')}</th> // [!code --]\n+ <th colSpan={header.colSpan} key={column.id}> // [!code ++]\n+   {flexRender( // [!code ++]\n+     header.column.columnDef.header, // [!code ++]\n+     header.getContext() // [!code ++]\n+   )} // [!code ++]\n+ </th> // [!code ++]\n```\n\n```tsx\n- <td {...cell.getCellProps()}>{cell.render('Cell')}</td> // [!code --]\n+ <td key={cell.id}> // [!code ++]\n+   {flexRender( // [!code ++]\n+     cell.column.columnDef.cell, // [!code ++]\n+     cell.getContext() // [!code ++]\n+   )} // [!code ++]\n+ </td> // [!code ++]\n```\n\n```tsx\n// in column definitions in this case\n- Header: ({ getToggleAllRowsSelectedProps }) => ( // [!code --]\n-   <input type=\"checkbox\" {...getToggleAllRowsSelectedProps()} /> // [!code --]\n- ), // [!code --]\n- Cell: ({ row }) => ( // [!code --]\n-   <input type=\"checkbox\" {...row.getToggleRowSelectedProps()} /> // [!code --]\n- ), // [!code --]\n+ header: ({ table }) => ( // [!code ++]\n+   <Checkbox // [!code ++]\n+     checked={table.getIsAllRowsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     indeterminate={table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     onChange={table.getToggleAllRowsSelectedHandler()} // [!code ++]\n+   /> // [!code ++]\n+ ), // [!code ++]\n+ cell: ({ row }) => ( // [!code ++]\n+   <Checkbox // [!code ++]\n+     checked={row.getIsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     disabled={!row.getCanSelect()} // [!code ++]\n+     indeterminate={row.getIsSomeSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     onChange={row.getToggleSelectedHandler()} // [!code ++]\n+   /> // [!code ++]\n+ ), // [!code ++]\n```\n\n### Other Changes\n\n- custom `filterTypes` (now called `filterFns`) have a new function signature as it only returns a boolean for whether the row should be included or not.\n\n```tsx\n- (rows: Row[], id: string, filterValue: any) => Row[] // [!code --]\n+ (row: Row, id: string, filterValue: any) => boolean // [!code ++]\n```\n\n- ...\n\n> This guide is a work in progress. Please consider contributing to it if you have time!\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Migrating to V8 Guide\n---\n\n## Migrating to V8\n\nTanStack Table V8 was a major rewrite of React Table v7 from the ground up in TypeScript. The overall structure/organization of your markup and CSS will largely remain the same, but many of the APIs have been renamed or replaced.\n\n### Notable Changes\n\n- Full rewrite to TypeScript with types included in the base package\n- Removal of plugin system to favor more inversion of control\n- Vastly larger and improved API (and new features like pinning)\n- Better controlled state management\n- Better support for server-side operations\n- Complete (but optional) data pipeline control\n- Agnostic core with framework adapters for React, Solid, Svelte, Vue, and potentially more in the future\n- New Dev Tools\n\n### Install the new Version\n\nThe new version of TanStack Table is published under the `@tanstack` scope. Install the new package using your favorite package manager:\n\n```bash\nnpm uninstall react-table @types/react-table\nnpm install @tanstack/react-table\n```\n\n```tsx\n- import { useTable } from 'react-table' // [!code --]\n+ import { useReactTable } from '@tanstack/react-table' // [!code ++]\n```\n\nTypes are now included in the base package, so you can remove the `@types/react-table` package.\n\n> If you want, you can keep the old `react-table` packages installed so that you can gradually migrate your code. You should be able to use both packages side-by-side for separate tables without any issues.\n\n### Update Table Options\n\n- Rename `useTable` to `useReactTable`\n- The old hook and plugin systems have been removed, but they have replaced with tree-shakable row model imports for each feature.\n\n```tsx\n- import { useTable, usePagination, useSortBy } from 'react-table'; // [!code --]\n+ import { // [!code ++]\n+   useReactTable, // [!code ++]\n+   getCoreRowModel, // [!code ++]\n+   getPaginationRowModel, // [!code ++]\n+   getSortedRowModel // [!code ++]\n+ } from '@tanstack/react-table'; // [!code ++]\n\n// ...\n\n-   const tableInstance = useTable( // [!code --]\n-     { columns,  data }, // [!code --]\n-     useSortBy, // [!code --]\n-     usePagination, //order of hooks used to matter // [!code --]\n-     // etc. // [!code --]\n-   ); // [!code --]\n+   const tableInstance = useReactTable({ // [!code ++]\n+     columns, // [!code ++]\n+     data, // [!code ++]\n+     getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(), // [!code ++]\n+     getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(), // [!code ++]\n+     getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(), //order doesn't matter anymore! // [!code ++]\n+     // etc. // [!code ++]\n+   }); // [!code ++]\n```\n\n- All `disable*` table options were renamed to `enable*` table options. (e.g. `disableSortBy` is now `enableSorting`, `disableGroupBy` is now `enableGrouping`, etc.)\n- ...\n\n### Update column definitions\n\n- accessor was renamed to either `accessorKey` or `accessorFn` (depending on whether you are using a string or function)\n- width, minWidth, maxWidth were renamed to size, minSize, maxSize\n- Optionally, you can use the new `createColumnHelper` function around each column definition for better TypeScript hints. (You can still just use an array of column definitions if you prefer.)\n  - The first parameter is the accessor function or accessor string.\n  - The second parameter is an object of column options.\n\n```tsx\nconst columns = [\n-  { // [!code --]\n-    accessor: 'firstName', // [!code --]\n-    Header: 'First Name', // [!code --]\n-  }, // [!code --]\n-  { // [!code --]\n-    accessor: row => row.lastName, // [!code --]\n-    Header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code --]\n-  }, // [!code --]\n\n// Best TypeScript experience, especially when using `cell.getValue()` later on\n+  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', { //accessorKey // [!code ++]\n+    header: 'First Name', // [!code ++]\n+  }), // [!code ++]\n+  columnHelper.accessor(row => row.lastName, { //accessorFn // [!code ++]\n+    header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code ++]\n+  }), // [!code ++]\n\n// OR (if you prefer)\n+ { // [!code ++]\n+   accessorKey: 'firstName', // [!code ++]\n+   header: 'First Name', // [!code ++]\n+ }, // [!code ++]\n+ { // [!code ++]\n+   accessorFn: row => row.lastName, // [!code ++]\n+   header: () => <span>Last Name</span>, // [!code ++]\n+ }, // [!code ++]\n]\n```\n\n> Note: If defining columns inside a component, you should still try to give the column definitions a stable identity. This will help with performance and prevent unnecessary re-renders. Store the column definitions in either a `useMemo` or `useState` hook.\n\n- Column Option Name Changes\n\n  - `Header` was renamed to `header`\n  - `Cell` was renamed to `cell` (The cell render function has also changed. See below)\n  - `Footer` was renamed to `footer`\n  - All `disable*` column options were renamed to `enable*` column options. (e.g. `disableSortBy` is now `enableSorting`, `disableGroupBy` is now `enableGrouping`, etc.)\n  - `sortType` `sortingFn`\n  - ...\n\n- Changes to custom cell renderers\n\n  - `value` was renamed `getValue` (Throughout the upgrade, instead of providing the value directly, a function `getValue` is exposed for evaluating the value. This change aims to improve performance by evaluating the value only when `getValue()` is called and then caching it.)\n  - `cell: { isGrouped, isPlaceholder, isAggregated }` is now `cell: { getIsGrouped, getIsPlaceholder, getIsAggregated }`\n  - `column`: The base level props are now RT-specific. Values that you added to the object when defining it are now one level deeper in `columnDef`.\n  - `table`: Props passed into the `useTable` hook now appear under `options`.\n\n### Migrate Table Markup\n\n- Use `flexRender()` instead of `cell.render('Cell')` or `column.render('Header')`, etc.\n- `getHeaderProps`, `getFooterProps`, `getCellProps`, `getRowProps`, etc. have all been _deprecated_.\n  - TanStack Table does not provide any default `style` or accessibility attributes like `role` anymore. These are still important for you to get right, but it had to be removed in order to support being framework-agnostic.\n  - You will need to define `onClick` handlers manually, but there are new `get*Handler` helpers to keep this simple.\n  - You will need to define the `key` props manually\n  - You will need to define the `colSpan` prop manually if using features that require it (grouped headers, aggregation, etc.)\n\n```tsx\n- <th {...header.getHeaderProps()}>{cell.render('Header')}</th> // [!code --]\n+ <th colSpan={header.colSpan} key={column.id}> // [!code ++]\n+   {flexRender( // [!code ++]\n+     header.column.columnDef.header, // [!code ++]\n+     header.getContext() // [!code ++]\n+   )} // [!code ++]\n+ </th> // [!code ++]\n```\n\n```tsx\n- <td {...cell.getCellProps()}>{cell.render('Cell')}</td> // [!code --]\n+ <td key={cell.id}> // [!code ++]\n+   {flexRender( // [!code ++]\n+     cell.column.columnDef.cell, // [!code ++]\n+     cell.getContext() // [!code ++]\n+   )} // [!code ++]\n+ </td> // [!code ++]\n```\n\n```tsx\n// in column definitions in this case\n- Header: ({ getToggleAllRowsSelectedProps }) => ( // [!code --]\n-   <input type=\"checkbox\" {...getToggleAllRowsSelectedProps()} /> // [!code --]\n- ), // [!code --]\n- Cell: ({ row }) => ( // [!code --]\n-   <input type=\"checkbox\" {...row.getToggleRowSelectedProps()} /> // [!code --]\n- ), // [!code --]\n+ header: ({ table }) => ( // [!code ++]\n+   <Checkbox // [!code ++]\n+     checked={table.getIsAllRowsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     indeterminate={table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     onChange={table.getToggleAllRowsSelectedHandler()} // [!code ++]\n+   /> // [!code ++]\n+ ), // [!code ++]\n+ cell: ({ row }) => ( // [!code ++]\n+   <Checkbox // [!code ++]\n+     checked={row.getIsSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     disabled={!row.getCanSelect()} // [!code ++]\n+     indeterminate={row.getIsSomeSelected()} // [!code ++]\n+     onChange={row.getToggleSelectedHandler()} // [!code ++]\n+   /> // [!code ++]\n+ ), // [!code ++]\n```\n\n### Other Changes\n\n- custom `filterTypes` (now called `filterFns`) have a new function signature as it only returns a boolean for whether the row should be included or not.\n\n```tsx\n- (rows: Row[], id: string, filterValue: any) => Row[] // [!code --]\n+ (row: Row, id: string, filterValue: any) => boolean // [!code ++]\n```\n\n- ...\n\n> This guide is a work in progress. Please consider contributing to it if you have time!\n"}
